    "issue_type": "drug_interaction",
    "message": "TDF can cause nephrotoxicity including chronic kidney disease and Fanconi syndrome. Concurrent NSAID use (ibuprofen) reduces renal perfusion via prostaglandin inhibition and can compound TDF-related renal injury. Patient already has trace proteinuria and low serum phosphate, suggesting possible early tubular dysfunction. The clinician's plan recommends PRN ibuprofen for back pain, which may accelerate renal harm in this context. Creatinine at 112 umol/L is within normal limits but does not exclude tubular damage.",
    "recommended_action": "Avoid or minimise ibuprofen use. Consider paracetamol-based pain management and evaluate renal tubular function before recommending NSAIDs.",
    "severity": "high",
    "title": "Ibuprofen with TDF increases nephrotoxicity risk"
  },
